// Title: PUA - CleanWipe Execution
// Sigma ID: f44800ac-38ec-471f-936e-3fa7d9c53100
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-12-18 | Modified: 2023-02-14
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects the use of CleanWipe a tool usually used to delete Symantec antivirus.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative use (Should be investigated either way)
// References:
//   - https://github.com/3CORESec/MAL-CL/tree/master/Descriptors/Other/CleanWipe
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_cleanwipe.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\SepRemovalToolNative_x64.exe" or (FolderPath endswith "\\CATClean.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "--uninstall") or (FolderPath endswith "\\NetInstaller.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-r") or (FolderPath endswith "\\WFPUnins.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/uninstall" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/enterprise"))
